<h1>Interviewer Training: STAR Method (2-Hour Module)</h1>
<h2>Agenda</h2>
<h3>Part 1: Why STAR? (20 min)</h3>
<p><strong>Learning objective:</strong> Understand why unstructured interviews fail and what STAR fixes.</p>
<ul><li>Problem: traditional interviews favor confident presenters over high performers</li><li>Research anchor: McDaniel et al. (1994) — structured behavioral interviews are ~2x more predictive</li><li>STAR as a predictive framework: past behavior predicts future behavior</li><li>Demo: same question, unstructured vs. STAR-probed — compare information yield</li></ul>
<p><strong>Discussion:</strong> What questions have you been asked that felt unfair or uninformative?</p>
<hr/>
<h3>Part 2: The STAR Flow (30 min)</h3>
<p><strong>Learning objective:</strong> Know each component and its prescribed probe when missing.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Good signal</th><th>Missing signal → probe</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Situation</td><td>Specific context, stakes, timeframe</td><td>&quot;Tell me more about the context — when was this?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Task</td><td>Clear personal responsibility</td><td>&quot;What was YOUR specific role?&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Action</td><td>First-person, multiple concrete steps</td><td>&quot;Walk me through exactly what YOU did.&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Result</td><td>Quantified outcome or clear impact</td><td>&quot;What was the end result? Can you quantify it?&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><strong>Common pitfalls:</strong></p>
<ul><li>Accepting &quot;we&quot; without probing for individual Action</li><li>Accepting hypotheticals (&quot;I would...&quot;)</li><li>Forgetting to close on Result</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h3>Part 3: Role-Play Practice (60 min)</h3>
<p><strong>Round 1 (20 min):</strong> Interviewer asks, candidate gives Scenario A (strong STAR)</p>
<ul><li>Score independently; compare; discuss variance</li></ul>
<p><strong>Round 2 (20 min):</strong> Interviewer asks, candidate gives Scenario B (missing Action)</p>
<ul><li>Practice probing for individual contribution</li><li>Score independently; compare</li></ul>
<p><strong>Round 3 (20 min):</strong> Interviewer asks, candidate gives Scenario C (weak/red-flag)</p>
<ul><li>Practice staying curious without leading</li><li>Score independently; debrief</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h3>Part 4: Q&amp;A and Calibration (10 min)</h3>
<ul><li>Review the scorecard template</li><li>Agree on behavioral anchor definitions for score 1, 3, 5 per competency</li><li>Confirm: independent submission before debrief channel opens</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h2>Pre-Training Materials</h2>
<p>Send 48 hours before:</p>
<ul><li>[ ] Role's competency table (4-6 competencies + weights)</li><li>[ ] This agenda</li><li>[ ] STAR one-pager (method summary)</li><li>[ ] Scorecard template</li></ul>
<h2>Post-Training Action Items</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] Each interviewer submits one practice scorecard for calibration (Scenario A)</li><li>[ ] Calibrator compares and flags divergence &gt; 1 point on any competency</li><li>[ ] Re-calibrate before live interviews if kappa &lt; 0.4</li></ul>
